# Docker build context for app/Dockerfile (context = repo root).
#
# Only app/, querying/, auto_query/, crawler_graph/ (+ their requirements files)
# are COPYed into the image; at runtime the whole project is bind-mounted over
# it (${PWD}:${PWD} in docker-compose.app.yml), so nothing else needs to be in
# the build context. Excluding the big/machine-local trees below keeps the
# first (cold) build from shipping ~1.3 GB to the daemon and avoids needless
# context re-scans. This file affects ONLY the root-context builds (the app +
# trainer images); the proxy services build from their own ./proxy/* contexts.

# Version control & local tooling (huge; never needed to build the image)
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.mcp.json

# Python virtualenvs & caches
venv
.venv
.venv-app
env
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache

# Node modules (untracked, unused by the image; ~235 MB)
node_modules

# Documentation & machine-local notes (not needed to build the image)
docs
*.md

# Template generator (heavy LoRA/model + scrape output; runs from the runtime
# bind mount, never baked into the image)
template_generator

# Machine-local deployment state & rendered/generated artifacts
.make
configs
website/sites
proxy/conf.d
proxy/certs
querying/runs
querying/provenance
crawler_graph/output

# Envs, logs, OS cruft
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
